// Repro (2026-11-20): an arpeggio beside a chord's held members only, not its @struck one.
// Kuecken Op.47-3 bar 70 (Fr. Kistner 1711), right hand: the wavy line stands beside the two white heads (gis, cis')
// and stops below the small black gis' on the same stem (@struck, request 31). The left hand has no arpeggio.
// What lysc (master 737c8dfb2) does with @arpeggio here: the line runs up beside the small gis' too, and the
// MusicXML puts <arpeggiate> on the gis' as well.
octave absolute
time 6/8
key b major
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }
section A {
  rh {
    repeat tremolo 24 { <gis cis' gis'@struck>64@arpeggio gis'64 } |
  }
  lh {
    repeat tremolo 24 { <e, e@struck>64 e64 } |
  }
}
score { staff rh staff lh }
